* indirect_dispatch -- sums 1..N through APPLY(<name held in a variable>, arg).
* bottleneck: BY-NAME dispatch to a SNOBOL-defined target; contrast with func_call
* (direct) and eval_fixed (EVAL).
* m4 status CORRECTED 2026-08-27: compiles, links, and runs clean, oracle-diffed
* ok in both modes on this tree.  The old "m4 SEGVs here, B1 class" claim (probe/b1,
* FINDING s156) no longer reproduces; README.md already carries the same correction
* (seat13, 2026-08-23) but this file's own header had not caught up.  The historical
* $FN(X) form this file used to carry is still ORACLE-INVALID (sbl raises ERROR 022)
* and is gone.
* Standalone:  scrip indirect_dispatch.sno   |   sbl -bf indirect_dispatch.sno
        &TRIM = 1
        &ANCHOR = 0
        &STLIMIT = -1
        DEFINE('ADD1(V)')                               :(ADD1_END)
ADD1    ADD1 = V + 1                                    :(RETURN)
ADD1_END
        ZFN = 'ADD1'
        DEFINE('INDIRECT_DISPATCH(N)')                  :(INDIRECT_DISPATCH_END)
INDIRECT_DISPATCH  ZI = 1
        ZS = 0
ZBL     ZS = ZS + APPLY(ZFN, ZI)
        ZI = LT(ZI, N) ZI + 1                           :S(ZBL)
        INDIRECT_DISPATCH = ZS                          :(RETURN)
INDIRECT_DISPATCH_END
*BENCH kernel=INDIRECT_DISPATCH check=500 bud=500 flr=20
        OUTPUT = 'dispatching through the name ' ZFN
        OUTPUT = 'APPLY(ZFN, 41) = ' APPLY(ZFN, 41)
        OUTPUT = 'sum of ADD1(1..500) = ' INDIRECT_DISPATCH(500)
END
